# EMZI Nexus — finish checklist

When completing **any** task that touches UI, API, auth, integrations, or deployment, verify against `docs/README.md` before saying the work is done.

## Always read first

- Index: `docs/README.md`
- UI/UX: `docs/DESIGN_TEMPLATE.md` (pass §28 pre-ship for UI work)

## Before marking complete

**Frontend / UI** (`frontend/src/**`):

- [ ] Semantic tokens only (`bg-card`, `text-foreground`) — no raw `slate-*` / `bg-white` on app pages
- [ ] shadcn/ui + Lucide; page title + description pattern (DESIGN_TEMPLATE §4.3)
- [ ] Back actions use `useGoBack` / `BackButton`, not hardcoded back links (§7.5)
- [ ] User decisions use `ConfirmDialog` before persist/delete/mode switch (§11.3)
- [ ] Mobile dialogs: `w-[calc(100vw-1.5rem)]`, horizontal footer on mobile (§11.9)
- [ ] Glass dock matches `docs/MOBILE_BOTTOM_NAV_DESIGN.md` if nav changed

**Backend / DB**:

- [ ] Integer PKs on app tables — no UUID primary keys (`docs/INITIAL_SETUP.md`)
- [ ] SSO changes match `docs/nexus-sso-setup.md`
- [ ] Webhook changes match `docs/event-webhook-setup.md`
- [ ] MCP routes under `/api/mcp/v1/` per `docs/emzi-nexus-mcp-catalog-spec.md`

**Deploy / env**:

- [ ] Split domains: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` points to API host (`docs/REACT_SPA_APACHE_HTACCESS.md`)

## Cleanup before marking complete

Always tidy every change made in the session — do not leave partial or exploratory edits behind.

- [ ] Remove debug code: `console.log`, `dd()`, `dump()`, temporary breakpoints, commented-out blocks
- [ ] Delete unused imports, variables, functions, and files introduced during the task
- [ ] Revert scratch/experimental edits that are not part of the delivered solution
- [ ] Match surrounding style: naming, formatting, and patterns in touched files
- [ ] Run linter on edited files; fix new issues introduced by the change
- [ ] Confirm no secrets, `.env` values, or one-off test data were added to tracked files

If cleanup reveals scope creep, trim the diff to what the task actually requires.

## Report format

End every completed task with two short sections (skip **Compliance** for docs-only or unrelated changes):

1. **Compliance** — what was verified against `docs/README.md` or what still needs manual QA
2. **Improvements** — concrete, optional follow-ups spotted while working (refactors, tests, perf, UX, docs, tech debt). Keep actionable; do not block delivery on items outside the request
